meta {
  name: Create Campaign
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/campaigns
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "Test Campaign Q3",
    "platform_name": "facebook",
    "status_name": "active",
    "budget": 50000,
    "started_at": "2026-06-01",
    "ended_at": "2026-09-30",
    "campaign_type_id": "{{campaignTypeId}}"
  }
}

docs {
  campaign_type_id is optional and CRM-only. Classifying a META campaign is not
  done here -- that mapping is per Meta campaign and tenant-wide, so it lives in
  meta-conversion-api, while this endpoint edits ONE BRANCH's record.

  Changing it relabels the campaign only; existing leads keep the type they were
  routed under. Moving the leads too is the reclassify fan-out's job.

  A campaign_type_id from another tenant is rejected with 400, never resolved.
}
